# ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │ PUZZLE 5 · Make the third harmonic sing              │
# └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
#
# Write a recipe (a shape function) where the 3rd harmonic
# is the loudest part of the sound. The note stays at
# 200 Hz, and the fundamental must still be audible.
#
# Only change the body of my_shape.
#
# Check:  edc/learn check 5      Hear:  edc/learn puzzle 5
#
#@ top 600 5 -- the 3rd harmonic (600 Hz) is the loudest
#@ peak 200 4 -30 -- the 200 Hz fundamental is still there

def my_shape(n, pf): 1.0 / n

play singer:
  additive(200, my_shape, 8) * 0.2

singer

